'''Andreæa''' (an-drē-ē′ä), ''n.'' [NL., named after G. R. ''Andreæ'', a German botanist. ''Andreæ'' was orig. gen. of LL. ''Andreas'', Andrew. See ''Andrew''.] A genus of mosses constituting the natural order ''Andreæaceæ'', intermediate between the ''Sphagnaceæ'' and the ''Bryaceæ'', or true mosses. {{smaller|It is distinguished by the longitudinal dehiscence of the capsule into four valves; otherwise it closely resembles the genus ''Grimmia''.}}
